 $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$" 13194139535629 true] [17592186162548 1100 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, P = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form $x^{T}Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P$." 13194139535629 false] [17592186162548 1145 "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358245 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358246 13194139535629 true] [17592186358245 1089 "q-140936" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358245 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535629 true] [17592186358245 1100 "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ in terms of the components of $y.$" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358245 1113 #uuid "101b0e7a-cd79-5786-8173-8a6700413fea" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358245 1145 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})^{2}+(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})-3({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & =8{y}_{1}^{2}-8{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{1}^{2}+3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}-3{y}_{1}^{2}-12{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-12{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =7{y}_{1}^{2}-17{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-12{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358247 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358248 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358249 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358250 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358251 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1041 "selection" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358250 13194139535629 true] [17592186358246 1110 #uuid "ce33c585-a739-5f29-809e-e0931a30db47" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358247 1034 "2{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{y}_{2}^{2}" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535629 true] [17592186358247 1111 #uuid "fa7b6b87-808b-57a6-b80d-026db8c60039" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358248 1034 "3{y}_{1}^{2}-13{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-13{y}_{2}^{2}" 13194139535629 true] [17592186358248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535629 true] [17592186358248 1111 #uuid "21cdaee9-e992-5da6-a